{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420754-designing-one-on-one-adventures-for-enduring-lockdown","id":1420754,"title":"Designing One On One Adventures for enduring lockdown","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-28T19:58:15-07:00","id":1420754,"title":"Designing One On One Adventures for enduring lockdown","content":"So, I aim to eventually put something on DriveThroughRPG with a nominal price tag. The setting must be tested in group play. This is postponed by the same ordeal everyone else is braving. I don't play by YouTube for the moment. I've definitely enjoyed some of the better Mage Chronicles up for view. With the thought of other players and STs all stuck in isolation, I am thinking of creating a One on One story to post with no price tag.<br /> <br /> 1. Investigate Location: Because a single character has a narrower selection of Spheres, investigating places is more of a challenge, especially if they are inhabited. You might have Matter and be able to scan the walls, but what does that tell you about the person in the next room? <br /> <br /> 2 - Growing your little empire: This could be for a Syndicate protagonist, or a Tradition Mage running a startup company or NGO. <br /> <br /> 3 - Putting those together - Pioneering: Investigate a location others fear to go, in the hopes of making it yours. The resources your little empire needs are there to be discovered. <br /> <br /> 4 - Personal struggle: Some merits and flaws come attached and the storyteller might keep some of the flaws secret for the first session or two. Nothing too punitive, but enough to encourage some good roleplaying.<br /> <br /> 5 - Chronicles of the Doomed - The player and storyteller agree that the character is doomed and the goal is to do their best for someone else or achieve something meaningful before death. <br /> <br /> Is there anything you would want in a One On One that you have never had the chance to play? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T20:31:51-07:00","id":1420759,"title":"","content":"Something on how to do a Seeking would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T21:36:00-07:00","id":1420765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420754-designing-one-on-one-adventures-for-enduring-lockdown?p=1420759#post1420759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something on how to do a Seeking would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dynamic/Questing/Pattern/Primordial?<br /> <br /> Where and when do you want to set it?<br /> <br /> Technocracy or Traditions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T22:18:06-07:00","id":1420770,"title":"","content":"If it is a series you could do one for each Avatar type. Most of the players I've had paid little attention to their Avatar type, so I don't have a personal preference.<br /> <br /> Technocracy and Traditions both need coverage with the M20 Technocracy Reloaded making the Technocracy updated to the 21st century.<br /> <br /> Modern-day setting would be the easiest. The location--should be set in an area the author knows well so that the adventure seems real and the Storyteller can be directed to some useful reading on the subject.<br /> <br /> To me, the key here would be to have a clear way to deconstruct the process so other Storytellers can apply it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T20:37:08-07:00","id":1420921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baakyocalder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1420754-designing-one-on-one-adventures-for-enduring-lockdown?p=1420770#post1420770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it is a series you could do one for each Avatar type. Most of the players I've had paid little attention to their Avatar type, so I don't have a personal preference.<br /> <br /> Technocracy and Traditions both need coverage with the M20 Technocracy Reloaded making the Technocracy updated to the 21st century.<br /> <br /> Modern-day setting would be the easiest. The location--should be set in an area the author knows well so that the adventure seems real and the Storyteller can be directed to some useful reading on the subject.<br /> <br /> To me, the key here would be to have a clear way to deconstruct the process so other Storytellers can apply it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The places I am most familiar with are boring as hell. Thank Gaia for the power of the internet. As for a process that can be deconstructed, I can give you one right now.<br /> <br /> Before getting into the process I use, I have to explain what options I don't and why. Paradox spirits can send you to a special realm that you have to escape. Umbral Lords occupy pocket dimensions. Seekings can be episodes where your Avatar puts you in a pocket realm to pass a test or learn something. I don't typically use trips to realms as Seekings, because there is so much demanded by the first two examples. <br /> <br /> Seekings, other than mini-realm tests, are the Avatar's expressed wish to change the World in some way, even if it is just in a small town. The four Essences are not neatly divided. Pattern and Dynamic are not even opposites. Having a Pattern Avatar doesn't make you someone without imagination or best advised to join the Technocracy. Pattern means you pursue smaller, achievable goals, often in series. It directs you to be a builder of reality, a pillar of the structures around you. <br /> <br /> A Pattern Avatar could give the following Seekings, in series:<br /> - Go to a city in India where there is intermittent loss of electricity and improve the electrical grid. <br /> - Build a power plant to meet increased demand.<br /> - Build a factory that pays wages so people can afford a better standard of living.<br /> <br /> A Dynamic Avatar giving Seekings in the same area:<br /> - Intervene in the life of a single person who has unrealized potential, but is stuck in a cycle of poverty. Change their life so they can become better and find original solutions to social problems faced by their neighbors, working with them.<br /> - Challenge a corrupt politician who exploits the poverty and enriches cronies. Win democratically and force the political establishment to take notice and Change accordingly.<br /> - Write an original screenplay to involve people who would benefit from entry into the film industry. <br /> <br /> A Questing Avatar in the same area:<br /> - Resolve the Kashmir Conflict so that there is permanent, un-interrupted peace. This is a huge goal that involves world-powers and geopolitics, exactly the kind of thing a Questing Avatar would thrust on the Mage. You might not achieve it, but are made better for trying.<br /> <br /> A Primordial Avatar in the same place:<br /> You are an incarnation of... Regret<br /> - Make the corrupt face the consequences of their crimes.<br /> - Help good people with unresolved guilt for things they could not entirely control, the regret having run its proper course.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-30T16:06:10-07:00","id":1421061,"title":"","content":"Those are some good ideas, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-04T16:05:36-08:00","id":1421867,"title":"","content":"I think the ideas are nice, thank you.<br /> <br /> As a one on one story, I think the quest of searching for a mentor/trainer could be interesting. <br /> It's a challenge many characters might face at some point. <br /> <br /> Or perhaps a story playing in a dream could be a way the storyteller doesn't have to take the place where the character is into account. Of course it would demand more work on the setting. <br /> <br /> I my own group one on one games have most of the time been opportunities for intense character play. <br /> So storytelling the interaction and beginning of a relationship (be it romance, friendship or professional) was the focus then. So it was an episode that could be the opportunity to get a new background or increase it (although this was in Vampire the Masquerade, but it might fit for Mage even better).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26246-caliginosa","name":"Caliginosa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}